#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Upper-garment integrated launcher for the dual-RoArm clothing-handling system.

This launcher keeps the validated FIX11 basket frontend and D50 perception
runtime in one Python process so they can share the same physical camera and
robot serial sessions. The active upper-garment workflow is:

  1) ARM2 basket pickup using the validated torque/contact grasp path.
  2) ARM2 arc placement onto the folding board.
  3) ARM1-preferred / ARM2-fallback centerward recenter correction.
  4) Fresh garment mask + upper-garment pose inference.
  5) Validate pose keypoints 7/8 near the expected board sides and move the
     grasp points inward from the garment boundary.
  6) Execute the dual grasp and paired mid-Z lift.
  7) Preserve board-X separation while synchronizing board-Y at the safe
     aerial height.
  8) Rise to the source high-Z state, replay the relative laydown trajectory,
     release the garment, and return both arms to taught standby.

The launcher transforms the validated FIX11 and D50 source text at runtime.
Those source-patch anchors, self-test markers, safety gates, model paths,
motion constants, CLI options, and runtime strings are therefore treated as
part of the executable contract and must not be reformatted casually.

Active learning/data-collection branches are disabled in the authoritative
runtime. The upper-garment pose engine remains enabled and is preflighted
before camera, serial, or robot startup.

Internal sibling runtime sources (feature-named dependency closure):
  - upper_basket_runtime.py
  - upper_board_runtime.py

D50's own runtime dependencies, camera calibration/configuration files,
Homography cache, basket calibration, segmentation engine, and upper-garment
pose engine must remain available at their resolved runtime paths.

Use --merge-self-test to validate FIX11/D50 source transformation and launcher
self-source invariants without starting physical robot motion.
"""

